  "estimatedMinutes": 1,
  "statement": "Each side of triangle \\(ABC\\) is \\(12\\) units. \\(D\\) is the foot of the perpendicular dropped from \\(A\\) on \\(BC,\\) and \\(E\\) is the midpoint of \\(AD.\\) The length of \\(BE,\\) in the same unit, is:",
  "answerChoices": [
    {
      "label": "A",
      "text": "\\(\\sqrt{18}\\)"
    },
    {
      "label": "B",
      "text": "\\(\\sqrt{28}\\)"
    },
    {
      "label": "C",
      "text": "\\(6\\)"
    },
    {
      "label": "D",
      "text": "\\(\\sqrt{63}\\)"
    },
    {
      "label": "E",
      "text": "\\(\\sqrt{98}\\)"
    }
  ],
